    "scenesThatPass": [
      "SEAMUS: I came to see if everything is all right.\nSEAMUS: You must be a Londrigan.\nMAURA: Yes, I am.",
      "SEAMUS: Yes. I'm sorry to call on you at this hour. You see, I knew Eliza well, and out of deference to her, I came by...to welcome you...and to ble…\nSEAMUS: ...at her request. She was a very religious woman.\nMAURA: Oh, that's nice...\nSEAMUS: May I come in?",
      "SEAMUS: Well yes I did. Lived here my whole life.\nAUBREY: Did you ever see a leprechaun?\nSEAMUS: A leprechaun? Well, let me tell you. They've been known to roam the land, and like it very much when you leave a bowl of milk out for them d…\nAUBREY: Can we leave out a bowl of milk, mommy?",
      "SEAMUS: Perhaps I'll see you in church.\nMAURA: Uh, we're not really practicing Catholics...\nSEAMUS: Well there's no time like the present. Good night.",
      "AUBREY: Mommy, the leprechauns drank the milk last night.\nMAURA: Well I bet you they're happy.\nAUBREY: Can I do it again tonight?\nMAURA: We'll have every leprechaun in Ireland here honey."
    ]
  },
